{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"guileless-emeritus-izuthrush","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Context\n- Epic 78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86 (Janitor Cleanup 2026-08-29) requires promoting the review scanner-integration lane from advisory to voting within the Gerrit Verified aggregate.\n- Incident 90c7 showed two failure classes to avoid: a vacuous Verified vote where a newly-required job did not run on its own introducing change, followed by a portability defect that made the lane red for every downstream change.\n- Promotion is now safe because the advisory lane is landed and validated green on real GitHub Actions (story aa9e-3d35-fd3e-41ee, CL 2666, merge SHA 4c9940348148fb255b17ddf1cb124701ad4565d7, run https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/33985796177), and bug b973-b298-9b5d-4765 closed the vacuous-vote escape with a predates-gate guard and lane-derived parity coverage on main.\n\nScope\n- Wire scanner-integration into automatic Gerrit Verified evaluation so it no longer depends on manual dispatch.\n- Add scanner-integration to .github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml voting needs, vote normalization, and workflow-conclusion aggregation so scanner failure blocks Verified.\n- Reverse the ADR-0114 advisory exception in scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py so mirror-vs-Verified parity requires scanner-integration in the voting aggregate.\n- Keep GitHub Actions and the Jenkins/mirror path coherent: _scanner-integration.yml, gerrit-verify.yaml, gerrit-scanner-verify.yml/test.yml parity, Jenkinsfile mirror behavior, and POSIX-dash-safe Make target semantics must remain aligned.\n- Update required coverage in tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py, tests/unit/test_workflow_names.py, tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py, tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py, and mechanism/parity baselines only as needed.\n\nAnti-90c7 safety design\n- Use the existing b973 predates-gate guard instead of trusting a vacuous vote. The promoted scanner-integration lane must be lane-derived into the guard/parity tests, and this change's own Verified run must show scanner-integration executed and passed before submit.\n- The promotion must not merely add the lane to the aggregate; it must ensure the lane runs automatically for every Gerrit patchset and that required-workflow aggregation observes its conclusion.\n- Portability guardrail: do not introduce bash-only shell options or a GitHub-only path. Keep the Make recipe and mirrored Jenkins/GHA semantics dash-safe and verified by parity tests.\n\nTesting\n- Held-out RED-first TDD: write acceptance coverage proving scanner-integration is now in the Verified aggregate and participates in the predates-gate/non-vacuous execution proof; hold out the edge/parity oracle while implementing.\n- Run targeted suites: tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py, tests/unit/test_workflow_names.py, tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py, tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py, scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py, scanner workflow/parity tests, mechanism-delta checks as applicable.\n- Run project gates with the worktree virtualenv first on PATH: make lint, make typecheck, and relevant tests. Deselect only the known macOS host-only failures if they appear in broader local runs.\n- Perform sandboxed mutation teeth by reintroducing the exact promoted-lane omission and confirming the held-out oracle returns RED, then restore.\n\nAcceptance Criteria\n- [ ] scanner-integration executes automatically on every Gerrit patchset as part of Verified evaluation, not only by manual dispatch.\n- [ ] gerrit-verify.yaml includes scanner-integration in voting needs, vote normalization, and required workflow-conclusion aggregation; a scanner failure blocks Verified.\n- [ ] scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py no longer treats scanner-integration as an ADR-0114 advisory exception; parity requires it in the voting aggregate.\n- [ ] Predates-gate/parity coverage includes scanner-integration and proves this promotion cannot pass on a vacuous vote where the new job did not execute on its own introducing change.\n- [ ] GitHub Actions, mirror test workflow, and Jenkins/mirror path remain coherent and POSIX-dash-safe; the incident-90c7 portability failure class does not recur.\n- [ ] Targeted scanner, parity, workflow-name, predates-guard, mechanism-delta, lint, typecheck, and relevant test gates pass locally with .venv/bin first on PATH.\n- [ ] Gerrit LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 are achieved, and this change's Verified run explicitly shows scanner-integration executed and passed (not skipped/vacuous) before submit.","id":"d645-8f51-0ff9-4070","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Promote scanner-integration lane from advisory to voting (Verified enforcement)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788636785013208001,"uuid":"6fc60fe4-a310-447c-bfaf-43d20674e352"}